  "ownership": [
    "NativeMountDomain belongs only to the exclusive command and process-view controllers. The descriptor-free spelling claim domain, backing, sealed data root, source reader and DICE values have no edge to it.",
    "Initial/rolling RW authority is consumed; FinalizeArchive/FinalizeProcess preserve actual backing mode and quotas, create no Execute record/index, and perform no cwd creation or payload execution.",
    "RO/NOSUID/NODEV are set and attested on the detached clone; original attached flags remain exactly unchanged and NOEXEC is absent so executable tools retain their file-mode semantics.",
    "Each RO use is linear and binds the exact executor request, physical root and fresh launch nonce. Mutable poisoned phases retain the last source backing and resource guards through worker cleanup on every error.",
    "Incoming views and returned successors transfer sequentially with bounded SCM rights. Root and every view successor validate before final payload ACK; pending tokens need the matching actual namespace/helper/monitor reap.",
    "Unchanged plan2MiB, maximum128 views, conservative511 scaffold component bound within existing512 inode mount, original scope/deadline, source banks, payload/control/FD and backing allowances remain finite. No copying, Host alias, proc reopen, detached data-FD clone or keeper fallback."
  ],
